            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "pokawa"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We make this every Christmas with a few changes. We use a box each of rice, corn &amp; wheat Chex plus a small bag of pretzels. To the sauce, we add about 25 shakes of Tabasco sauce for a little kick plus 1/4th c soy sauce. We also use cashews and peanuts. Everyone loves it. Also since Furikake is hard to find around here we get it on Amazon.",
            "datePublished": "2018-12-27T10:44:41.373Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Laurahallie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This snack was easy to make and was a good use of my jar of furikake. I do think it would be nice to add some soy sauce, as I’m used to having a savory Chex mix and this was quite sweet. I only used half of the cereal called for in the recipe as my baking sheet could only handle the one box.",
